course: dictionary
lesson: 12736
title: Describing words: drooping
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Drooping means hanging or bending down. Plants droop when they are thirsty or too hot, and people can droop when they are tired or weak. Look for the clues around the word to work out what it means.
explain: «The flowers were drooping in the hot sun.» The sun is hot and the flowers hang down, so drooping means bending down because they need water. Try the swap test: put «hanging down» in place of drooping, and if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Drooping can also describe feelings. «Her drooping spirits lifted when the bell rang.» Spirits here means mood, so drooping spirits means feeling sad or low on energy. A writer uses drooping to paint a picture: «drooping shoulders» show someone tired or sad.
fact: Drooping means hanging or bending down, often because of weakness, tiredness or lack of water.
fact: Droop is a verb: droop, droops, drooped, drooping.
fact: Drooping can also be a describing word, as in «drooping flowers».
fact: «Drooping spirits» means losing energy or feeling sad.
fact: In science, drooping leaves can be a sign that a plant needs water or is too hot.
exercise: «The flowers were drooping in the hot sun, so Mia gave them a drink.» What does drooping mean here? | Shining brightly | Singing loudly | Growing very tall | *Hanging down because they need water
exercise: «Grandad sat with drooping shoulders after the long day.» What do drooping shoulders show? | He was dancing | He was ready to run a race | *He was tired or sad | He was very cold and happy
exercise: What is the -ing form of droop? | Droop | *Drooping | Drooped | Droops
test: «Her drooping eyelids showed she was ready for bed.» What do drooping eyelids show? | She had lost her glasses | She was excited to start the race | *She was tired | She was singing
test: In which phrase is drooping a describing word? | «they drooped yesterday» | «is drooping over the desk» | *«drooping flowers» | «he droops every day»
exam: Mia says drooping spirits means happy spirits. Is she right? | *No, drooping spirits means losing energy or feeling sad | Yes, because spirits are always happy | Yes, drooping means cheerful | No, it means moving very fast
